  "body": "The default-machine preflight runs before the per-operation post can add its operation name. The old message names Setup2 and the missing default machine file. It omits Face2. The CLI refuses and writes no NC.\n\nKeep the affected operation names in the same refusal as their setups and the underlying machine-file error. The preflight already collected these operations in posting order. The regression now checks the setup, the unmounted operation, the filename and the empty output directory. It excludes the mounted Face1.\n\nUntouched main at 1d81b609c reproduced the failure of a_missing_default_machine_file_refuses_the_post_per_operation. The #2948 trial on that main also reproduced it. The original missing-file refusal from #2319 is retained.\n\nThe full quick gate passed all 251 steps on d0fe169a1 in 36.4 minutes on macOS arm64. All nine tests in default_machine_missing passed on this head. They also passed on the trial merge with #2948. The complete reached heavy gate passed all 196 steps in 51.6 minutes. The gate commands were `cargo xtask gate quick --base 1d81b609c` and `cargo xtask gate heavy --base 1d81b609c`. No physical machine was used.\n\nEffort: high\nChangelog: A missing default machine file now identifies the affected operation and setup when posting separate NC files.\n\nFixes #3089\n\n",
